WEBVTT

NOTE station-details: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.606
Some stations drive
more than one sprinkler.

V0-2
00:00:04.706 --> 00:00:07.920
Expand the row to see what each
sprinkler actually measured.

V1a-1
00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:14.502
A chevron beside the
station name means the

V1a-2
00:00:14.602 --> 00:00:17.100
station has more than one
sprinkler paired to it.

V1b-1
00:00:19.376 --> 00:00:22.136
Without the chevron,
the row is the whole story.

V2a-1
00:00:28.246 --> 00:00:31.347
Each child row is named for
its parent and numbered,

V2a-2
00:00:31.447 --> 00:00:35.026
and carries its own scan date
and its own measured moisture.

V2b-1
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.708
Nothing else is editable
at sprinkler level.

V2b-2
00:00:39.808 --> 00:00:42.560
The target and the adjustment
belong to the station.

V3a-1
00:00:49.853 --> 00:00:54.213
The station's Avg. VWC is the
average of its sprinklers' readings.

V3b-1
00:00:56.536 --> 00:01:01.773
Two sprinklers reading 31.4 and
30.4 give a station average of 30.9,

V3b-2
00:01:01.873 --> 00:01:06.726
and a station that looks fine
can still hide one dry sprinkler.

V4a-1
00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:16.092
A child whose scan is
older than today shows a

V4a-2
00:01:16.192 --> 00:01:19.315
modeled value marked with
an orange calculator icon,

V4a-3
00:01:19.415 --> 00:01:23.200
and the parent average is then
part measurement and part model.

V4b-1
00:01:25.513 --> 00:01:29.003
The parent row carries a gray
calculator icon beside its average,

V4b-2
00:01:29.103 --> 00:01:31.573
so you can tell it
includes a modeled reading.
